\par
6. THE LIVING PORTRAIT (the signature of this page)\par
\par
The portrait is a floating 3D-animated head of an adult Korean woman with shoulder-length dark-brown hair, pearl earrings and a soft smile. She feels alive. It is built from 59 separately generated pictures of the same face, all pixel-aligned, swapped on a soft stretchy sheet in WebGL. Use the exact picture ids in the code below. Do not fake expressions with code.\par
\par
Hard rules, because each of these was a real bug:\par
- Only ONE picture is ever on screen. Never composite eye patches, hair masks or overlays over a face: they cause double eyes, double chins, black outlines and spots. Changes between pictures are a crossfade of 70ms at most.\par
- Gaze is whole pictures, 16 directions plus half and closed lids.\par
- The sheet must never fold. Overlapping triangles draw as a comb of cuts, so every frame each row and column is forced back into order with a minimum gap (the untangle step). The hand's radius and pull limit are also chosen so the slope cannot fold.\par
- Physics runs at a fixed 1/240s step whatever the frame rate, otherwise it tears into spikes on large screens.\par
- She never changes her expression on her own while the visitor is active. Self-playing acts only start after 30 to 45 seconds with no input, and any input ends them at once.\par
\par
Behaviour:\par
- Page load: her eyes are closed. The first pointer move wakes her through half to open.\par
- Moving the cursor: her eyes follow it in 16 directions everywhere on the page, and she blinks every 2.2 to 5.6 seconds. Her head leans slightly toward the cursor.\par
- Hover, reacting after 80ms: lips kiss, nose goes cross-eyed, either eye winks. The forehead, cheeks, chin and hair do not change her face on hover; her eyes keep following.\par
- Tap: forehead angry, eyes ouch, nose plays the sneeze act, lips tongue out, cheek puffed, chin laugh.\par
- Tap on hair: cycles pink, blue, blonde and back to her own hair. Colours persist. The colour pictures face forward, so her eyes rest while coloured, and expressions show her own hair.\par
- Grab and pull anywhere: the skin stretches like dough and ripples back. Pull distance moves her from shock to ouch to scared. On release she looks scrunched or dizzy; after 5 pulls in 14 seconds she gets angry, after 8 she cries.\par
- Shaking the cursor fast blows her hair, and keeping it up turns her sick.\par
- Hovering the Contact Me button gives heart eyes, and leaving it gives a grin.\par
- Scrolling makes her look down.\par
- Idle acts, in rotation: yawn, shifty eyes, a gum bubble that pops on her face, a fly that lands on her nose and is blown off, flirt, eye roll, sneeze, trying on hair colours, a ghost hand tugging her cheek, cross-eyed fish face, whistle, dozing off and snoring, cheeky tongue, starry eyes, and crying.\par
